      "message": "fix(project): a typed hole floor no longer reads Stale after save and reopen\n\nThe Drill, Bore and Thread arms of the op stamp digest each hole (and\nradial hole) through operation::hole_digest, which snaps every hole float\nto the 1 um lattice the project file stores it on (HoleDto/CrossHoleDto).\nA floor typed as 3.8099999999999996 mm and the 3.81 the file reloads now\nstamp alike, so an op saved Ok reopens Ok. On-lattice holes hash exactly\nas before; half a micron or more still moves the stamp. Same remedy as\n#1351's path signature. Decision in docs/decisions/1560-hole-digest-lattice.md.\n\nFixes #1560\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
